    Skeptic's fix: walk binds every component's object expressions before any component's top-level variables

    Edits the original tree. Row 648's repair bound a component's object
    expressions before its own top-level variables, but the driver initializes
    the components' variables one component after another, so a top-level
    variable that reads an imported component's object expression, through
    that component's top-level variable or a function, still stopped at load
    with 'Missing value: *objectexpr_ObjectExpr'. CUWrapper.initObjectExprs
    binds a component's constructors once; Driver.evalComponent calls it for
    every component before the loop of initVars, which still calls it for a
    component the driver did not reach.

    Test: tests/ObjectExpressionImportedVariableWalk.fss with its helper
    test_library/ObjectExpressionVariableLib.fsi/.fss, red on the worker's
    head 8803d2f45's build (harness, 12:47:07Z), green on the fix (12:48:48Z).

    Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
